# NestJS Backend Development Rules

## Core Principles

- **TypeScript First**: Always use strict TypeScript configuration with proper typing
- **Dependency Injection**: Leverage NestJS DI container for all services and controllers
- **Decorator Pattern**: Use NestJS decorators consistently for metadata and configuration
- **Module Organization**: Follow NestJS module structure and separation of concerns

## File Structure & Organization

```
src/
├── modules/           # Feature modules (users, lessons, avatars, etc.)
│   ├── users/
│   │   ├── dto/      # Data Transfer Objects
│   │   ├── entities/ # Database entities/models
│   │   ├── users.controller.ts
│   │   ├── users.service.ts
│   │   ├── users.module.ts
│   │   └── users.resolver.ts  # GraphQL resolver
├── common/            # Shared utilities, guards, interceptors
├── config/            # Configuration files
├── database/          # Database connection and migrations
└── main.ts           # Application entry point
```

## Naming Conventions

- **Files**: kebab-case (e.g., `user-profile.service.ts`)
- **Classes**: PascalCase (e.g., `UserProfileService`)
- **Methods**: camelCase (e.g., `getUserProfile`)
- **Constants**: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE (e.g., `MAX_LOGIN_ATTEMPTS`)
- **Interfaces**: PascalCase with 'I' prefix for internal interfaces (e.g., `IUserRepository`)

## Service Layer Rules

- **Single Responsibility**: Each service should have one clear purpose
- **Dependency Injection**: Inject dependencies through constructor, never use `new`
- **Async Operations**: Always use async/await, avoid callbacks
- **Error Handling**: Use custom exception filters and proper HTTP status codes

```typescript
@Injectable()
export class UserService {
  constructor(
    private readonly userRepository: IUserRepository,
    private readonly logger: Logger,
    private readonly configService: ConfigService
  ) {}

  async createUser(createUserDto: CreateUserDto): Promise<User> {
    try {
      const user = await this.userRepository.create(createUserDto);
      this.logger.log(`User created: ${user.id}`);
      return user;
    } catch (error) {
      this.logger.error(`Failed to create user: ${error.message}`);
      throw new InternalServerErrorException('Failed to create user');
    }
  }
}
```

## Controller Rules

- **Validation**: Always use DTOs with class-validator decorators
- **Response Types**: Define explicit return types for all endpoints
- **Error Handling**: Use proper HTTP status codes and exception filters
- **Documentation**: Include OpenAPI/Swagger decorators for API documentation

```typescript
@Controller('users')
@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard)
@ApiTags('users')
export class UsersController {
  constructor(private readonly usersService: UsersService) {}

  @Post()
  @HttpCode(201)
  @UsePipes(new ValidationPipe({ transform: true }))
  async create(@Body() createUserDto: CreateUserDto): Promise<UserResponseDto> {
    return this.usersService.createUser(createUserDto);
  }
}
```

## DTO & Validation Rules

- **Input Validation**: Use class-validator decorators for all input validation
- **Type Safety**: Create separate DTOs for create, update, and response operations
- **Transformation**: Use class-transformer for data transformation
- **Nested Objects**: Validate nested objects with proper DTOs

```typescript
export class CreateUserDto {
  @IsEmail()
  @IsNotEmpty()
  email: string;

  @IsString()
  @MinLength(8)
  @Matches(/^(?=.*[a-z])(?=.*[A-Z])(?=.*\d)/)
  password: string;

  @IsString()
  @IsNotEmpty()
  @MinLength(2)
  firstName: string;

  @IsString()
  @IsNotEmpty()
  @MinLength(2)
  lastName: string;
}
```

## Database & Entity Rules

- **TypeORM**: Use TypeORM decorators consistently
- **Relationships**: Define clear entity relationships with proper cascade options
- **Indexing**: Add database indexes for frequently queried fields
- **Soft Deletes**: Implement soft deletes for user data when appropriate

```typescript
@Entity('users')
@Index(['email'], { unique: true })
export class User {
  @PrimaryGeneratedColumn('uuid')
  id: string;

  @Column({ unique: true })
  email: string;

  @Column()
  passwordHash: string;

  @CreateDateColumn()
  createdAt: Date;

  @UpdateDateColumn()
  updatedAt: Date;

  @DeleteDateColumn()
  deletedAt?: Date;
}
```

## Configuration & Environment

- **Environment Variables**: Use ConfigService for all configuration
- **Validation**: Validate environment variables at startup
- **Secrets**: Store sensitive data in AWS Secrets Manager
- **Environment Files**: Use .env files for local development only
- **Node.js Version**: Use Node.js 22 (latest AWS Lambda supported version)
- **Package Manager**: Use pnpm for dependency management and faster installations

```typescript
@Module({
  imports: [
    ConfigModule.forRoot({
      isGlobal: true,
      validationSchema: Joi.object({
        NODE_ENV: Joi.string().valid('development', 'production', 'test'),
        PORT: Joi.number().default(3000),
        DATABASE_URL: Joi.string().required(),
      }),
    }),
  ],
})
export class AppModule {}
```

## Logging & Monitoring

- **Structured Logging**: Use Winston or Pino with structured log format
- **Log Levels**: Use appropriate log levels (error, warn, info, debug)
- **Context**: Include request context in logs (user ID, request ID, etc.)
- **Performance**: Log execution time for critical operations

```typescript
@Injectable()
export class LoggerService {
  private logger = new Logger(LoggerService.name);

  logUserAction(userId: string, action: string, metadata?: any) {
    this.logger.log({
      message: `User action: ${action}`,
      userId,
      action,
      metadata,
      timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
    });
  }
}
```

## Security Rules

- **Authentication**: Use JWT tokens with proper expiration
- **Authorization**: Implement role-based access control (RBAC)
- **Input Sanitization**: Validate and sanitize all user inputs
- **Rate Limiting**: Implement rate limiting for public endpoints
- **CORS**: Configure CORS properly for production

```typescript
@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard, RolesGuard)
@Roles(UserRole.ADMIN)
@Controller('admin')
export class AdminController {
  // Admin-only endpoints
}
```

## Performance Rules

- **Database Queries**: Use query optimization and proper indexing
- **Caching**: Implement Redis caching for frequently accessed data
- **Async Operations**: Use Promise.all for parallel operations when possible
- **Memory Management**: Avoid memory leaks in long-running processes
- **Connection Pooling**: Configure proper database connection pooling
